# Table 6: moving vs fixed feature particles on Stanford scans. Configuration: 6 levels (base 16, finest 512),
# curvature thresholds [0,8,16,32,64,128], 3M oriented samples. moving = n_proj=3 projection rounds move the feature particles
# onto the surface); fixed = n_proj=0 (feature particles stay at the cell centres). --curv_mode mesh: the Table 6 lines assign the
# grid levels from the cotan mesh curvature; with the default robust curvature the armadillo gets 83k instead of 115k feature
# particles. --time_rebuild also reports the warm rebuild time (the build / query columns of the table). Commands run from the
# repository root; scripts/launch.py appends --out runs/<name>.
